   334	<section id="who-feels-it">
   335	<p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">What changes in practice</p>
   336	<h2 data-layer="fact">The plaintiffs get warning; the parties dispute the immediate safety closure</h2>
   337	<p data-layer="narrative">The reproduced order gives the plaintiffs in both cases a warning period before the defendants implement a covered project-scope change. It adds written notice to the earlier pledge to report a reversal of the no-demolition position.<sup class="src-ref">
   338	<a href="#src-21" data-record-href="/records/upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="provide such notice in writing to Plaintiffs in both cases" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a>
   339	</sup>
   340	<sup class="src-ref">
   341	<a href="#src-7" data-record-href="/records/preservation-joint-report-62-2026-08-28/" data-passage="change in the Board’s plans that would constitute a reversal" aria-label="Source 7: read the evidence">7</a>
   342	</sup>
   343	</p>
   344	<p data-layer="narrative">The May opinion records Floca's estimate that between 75 and 175 of roughly 300 employees would be affected by the closure. It also says several performance contracts would be affected, the Center had laid off at least 2 groups of staff including programming personnel, and 10 programming staff remained.<sup class="src-ref">
   345	<a href="#src-10" data-record-href="/records/beatty-opinion-50-2026-05-29/" data-passage="75 to 175 of roughly 300 employees at the Center would be affected" aria-label="Source 10: read the evidence" data-passages="The closure will affect several existing performance contracts&#10;laid off at least two tranches of staff members&#10;just ten members of the programming staff remain">10</a>
   346	</sup>
   347	</p>
   348	<p data-layer="narrative">The opinion also identifies lost ticket and tourist revenue, trouble retaining audiences, the possible permanent loss of specialized arts professionals and long-term donor attrition among the downsides described in sworn testimony.<sup class="src-ref">
   349	<a href="#src-10" data-record-href="/records/beatty-opinion-50-2026-05-29/" data-passage="lost ticket and tourist revenue; chronic challenges in audience retention" aria-label="Source 10: read the evidence" data-passages="potentially permanent loss of highly-specialized arts professionals; and long-term attrition of donors">10</a>
   350	</sup>
   351	</p>
   352	<p data-layer="narrative">The August board plan keeps the REACH, the Center's expansion campus, open for educational and artistic programming, supports National Symphony Orchestra performances at off-site venues, and moves the Kennedy Center Honors and Mark Twain Prize off site while the main building is closed.<sup class="src-ref">
   353	<a href="#src-10" data-record-href="/records/beatty-opinion-50-2026-05-29/" data-passage="expansion campus, known as the REACH" aria-label="Source 10: read the evidence">10</a>
   354	</sup>
   355	<sup class="src-ref">
   356	<a href="#src-13" data-record-href="/records/board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13/" data-passage="shall continue to present educational and artistic programming at the REACH" aria-label="Source 13: read the evidence" data-passages="those performances offsite&#10;Kennedy Center Honors and the Mark Twain Prize for American Humor">13</a>
   357	</sup>
   358	</p>
   359	<p data-layer="narrative">In a public statement, the 8 preservation plaintiffs said the court should consider a receiver or replacement leadership if the Center's leaders would not protect the building. They also named a limited receiver, independent monitor or other neutral officer. They framed those measures as steps for the court to consider.<sup class="src-ref">
   360	<a href="#src-32" data-record-href="/records/preservation-plaintiffs-statement-2026-09-17/" data-passage="the court should consider appointing a receiver or replacing that leadership" aria-label="Source 32: read the evidence" data-passages="a receiver, limited receiver, independent monitor, or other neutral officer">32</a>
   361	</sup>
   362	</p>
   363	<p data-layer="narrative">The defendants called the September 16 safety closure separate from the renovation decision. Beatty's reply answered with a chronology: the building remained open for 12 days after the September 4 plaster fall, the Walter P Moore analysis dated from June and July, and the defendants identified no meaningfully new information between the incident and the closure. The closure came the day after the board vote.<sup class="src-ref">
   364	<a href="#src-4" data-record-href="/records/defendants-response-86-2026-09-17/" data-passage="separate from any Board decision related to closure for ongoing renovations" aria-label="Source 4: read the evidence">4</a>
   365	</sup>
   366	<sup class="src-ref">
   367	<a href="#src-6" data-record-href="/records/beatty-reply-87-2026-09-17/" data-passage="kept the building open for twelve days after September 4" aria-label="Source 6: read the evidence" data-passages="identified no meaningfully new information&#10;was completed in June and July of 2026&#10;immediately followed the Board’s closure vote">6</a>
   368	</sup>
   369	</p>
   370	<p data-layer="narrative">Floca identified two immediate safety grounds: an engineering assessment of the roof-terrace canopy and the September 4 failure of a five-by-four-foot piece of ceiling plaster after water damage. The same declaration reported severe corrosion in 46 of 278 panels and said one-third of the panels required immediate replacement.<sup class="src-ref">
   371	<a href="#src-5" data-record-href="/records/floca-declaration-86-1-2026-09-17/" data-passage="a roof terrace canopy assessment" aria-label="Source 5: read the evidence" data-passages="failure of a five-by-four-foot piece of one-inch-thick ceiling plaster on September 4&#10;severe corrosion in 46 panels&#10;One-third of all panels require immediate replacement">5</a>
   372	</sup> Cooper denied the requested hearing. Neither UPI's reproduced order text nor counsel's release reports a resolution of the parties' factual dispute.<sup class="src-ref">
   373	<a href="#src-21" data-record-href="/records/upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="Beatty's request for a hearing was denied" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a>
   374	</sup>
   375	<sup class="src-ref">
   376	<a href="#src-18" data-record-href="/records/beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17/" data-passage="Judge Cooper additionally ordered discovery" aria-label="Source 18: read the evidence">18</a>
   377	</sup>
   378	</p>
   379	<p data-layer="narrative">Bridget Kennedy-Bailey, whose declaration supported Beatty's motion, said she saw fencing block the building and saw a forklift hit exterior pillars several times. That observation was sworn testimony from one witness, not a finding by the court.<sup class="src-ref">
   380	<a href="#src-2" data-record-href="/records/kennedy-bailey-declaration-84-1-2026-09-16/" data-passage="Bridget Kennedy-Bailey" aria-label="Source 2: read the evidence" data-passages="forklift run into and hit the pillars">2</a>
   381	</sup>
   382	</p>
   383	<p data-layer="narrative">The board's August minutes record 26 votes cast: 23 in favor and 3 opposed. Another 2 trustees were present but did not vote, and several were absent. The resolution directed closure of the main building for restoration and renovation and authorized legal steps to dissolve the injunction that prevented that closure.<sup class="src-ref">
   384	<a href="#src-13" data-record-href="/records/board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13/" data-passage="Motion carried by roll call, 23 in favor, 3 opposed" aria-label="Source 13: read the evidence" data-passages="Present, not voting&#10;seeking to dissolve the preliminary injunction">13</a>
   385	</sup>
   386	</p>
   387	<p data-layer="narrative">That vote came with acknowledged gaps. Beatty said she received 2 slides 2 days before the meeting, Whitehouse listed 6 baseline requirements, and Larsen said the board lacked the full four-year analysis. The defendants later said the full Delta report went to trustees on August 31.<sup class="src-ref">
   388	<a href="#src-13" data-record-href="/records/board-minutes-68-3-2026-08-13/" data-passage="only two PowerPoint slides, received two days prior" aria-label="Source 13: read the evidence" data-passages="summarizing his request in six points&#10;characterized these as baseline requirements&#10;did not have the full four-year analysis">13</a>
   389	</sup>
   390	<sup class="src-ref">
   391	<a href="#src-28" data-record-href="/records/defendants-statement-facts-89-2-2026-09-18/" data-passage="On August 31, the Center’s management distributed the finalized Delta Consulting" aria-label="Source 28: read the evidence">28</a>
   392	</sup>
   393	</p>
   394	</section>
   395	<section id="outlets">
   396	<p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">Cross-source check</p>
   397	<h2 data-layer="fact">What the coverage got right, and what it got wrong</h2>
   398	<p data-layer="fact">The notice-order check uses 6 coverage records. 3 receive verdict cards below. ABC supplied the status-report detail and the placard limitation; CBS carried the Center's no-demolition response; and the earlier USA Today report carried Trump's ripped-down remark, which was checked against the filing that put it before the court. Another 2 AP reports document the next-day protest and Trump's response to a demolition question.<sup class="src-ref">
   399	<a href="#src-19" data-record-href="/records/abc-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="update him on the status" aria-label="Source 19: read the evidence" data-passages="The published images don't show the entire placard">19</a>
   400	</sup>
   401	<sup class="src-ref">
   402	<a href="#src-26" data-record-href="/records/cbs-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="nothing is being demolished" aria-label="Source 26: read the evidence">26</a>
   403	</sup>
   404	<sup class="src-ref">
   405	<a href="#src-22" data-record-href="/records/usa-today-kennedy-center-comments-2026-09-16/" data-passage="end up being ripped down" aria-label="Source 22: read the evidence">22</a>
   406	</sup>
   407	<sup class="src-ref">
   408	<a href="#src-3" data-record-href="/records/beatty-notice-85-2026-09-17/" data-passage="it will end up being ripped down" aria-label="Source 3: read the evidence">3</a>
   409	</sup>
   410	<sup class="src-ref">
   411	<a href="#src-33" data-record-href="/records/ap-kennedy-center-protest-2026-09-18/" data-passage="Thousands of people joined outside" aria-label="Source 33: read the evidence">33</a>
   412	</sup>
   413	<sup class="src-ref">
   414	<a href="#src-35" data-record-href="/records/ap-trump-kennedy-center-2026-09-18/" data-passage="did not directly respond when a reporter asked whether he planned to demolish the theater" aria-label="Source 35: read the evidence">35</a>
   415	</sup>
   416	</p>
   417	<div data-layer="fact">
   418	<article class="outlet-check warn">
