   477	<section id="claim-check">
   478	<p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The headline claim</p>
   479	<h2 data-layer="fact">Claim checked against the record</h2>
   480	<div data-layer="fact">
   481	<div class="contested-block">
   482	<p class="cb-label">The judge said Trump must give 30 days&#39; notice before demolishing the Kennedy Center</p>
   483	<p>Directionally right, but incomplete. The order binds the defendants and requires written notice to the plaintiffs in both cases more than 30 days before implementing a change to the scope of the project plans previously presented to the court, including demolition. It does not identify a demolition plan, decide whether one would be lawful or impose a general notice rule for every physical change.<sup class="src-ref">
   484	<a href="#src-21" data-record-href="/records/upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="more than 30 days before the implementation of any changes to the scope of the project plans presented to the Court" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a>
   485	</sup>
   486	</p>
   487	</div>
   488	</div>
   489	</section>
   490	<section id="what-happened-next">
   491	<p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">The next dated steps</p>
   492	<h2 data-layer="fact">The closure and renovation claims moved onto separate tracks</h2>
   493	<p data-layer="narrative">The existing scheduling order had already opened expedited discovery on Beatty's closure claim. It set September 23 deadlines for written discovery requests and deposition notices, September 30 for written responses, October 7 for completed depositions and October 9 for the close of discovery.<sup class="src-ref">
   494	<a href="#src-15" data-record-href="/records/scheduling-order-82-2026-09-16/" data-passage="Requests for Written and Document Discovery" aria-label="Source 15: read the evidence" data-passages="All Discovery Closed">15</a>
   495	</sup>
   496	</p>
   497	<p data-layer="narrative">The September 17 order added the update and advance-notice requirements. The September 16 scheduling order separately set deadlines for a motion to vacate the preliminary injunction and for discovery on the closure claim.<sup class="src-ref">
   498	<a href="#src-18" data-record-href="/records/beatty-counsel-reaction-2026-09-17/" data-passage="required the Board to update the Court by September 23" aria-label="Source 18: read the evidence">18</a>
   499	</sup>
   500	<sup class="src-ref">
   501	<a href="#src-21" data-record-href="/records/upi-kennedy-center-2026-09-17/" data-passage="more than 30 days before the implementation" aria-label="Source 21: read the evidence">21</a>
   502	</sup>
   503	<sup class="src-ref">
   504	<a href="#src-15" data-record-href="/records/scheduling-order-82-2026-09-16/" data-passage="Motion to Vacate the Preliminary" aria-label="Source 15: read the evidence">15</a>
   505	</sup>
   506	</p>
   507	<p data-layer="narrative">On September 18, the defendants filed a motion to dissolve the May preliminary injunction and a renewed motion for partial summary judgment on Beatty's remaining closure and construction claims. Those motions asked the court for relief; they did not themselves dissolve the injunction or decide the claims.<sup class="src-ref">
   508	<a href="#src-24" data-record-href="/records/defendants-motion-vacate-88-2026-09-18/" data-passage="DEFENDANTS’ MOTION TO DISSOLVE PRELIMINARY INJUNCTION" aria-label="Source 24: read the evidence">24</a>
   509	</sup>
   510	<sup class="src-ref">
   511	<a href="#src-25" data-record-href="/records/defendants-summary-judgment-89-2026-09-18/" data-passage="DEFENDANTS’ RENEWED MOTION FOR" aria-label="Source 25: read the evidence">25</a>
   512	</sup>
   513	</p>
   514	<p data-layer="narrative">Floca says management distributed a packet on September 13 for discussion at the September 15 board meeting and attached it to his declaration as Exhibit B. The declaration dates the packet to the closure deliberations but does not reproduce its contents or identify the recognition proposal.<sup class="src-ref">
   515	<a href="#src-29" data-record-href="/records/floca-declaration-89-3-2026-09-18/" data-passage="On September 13, 2026, the Center distributed to trustees a packet of materials" aria-label="Source 29: read the evidence" data-passages="attached to this declaration as Exhibit B">29</a>
   516	</sup>
   517	</p>
   518	<p data-layer="narrative">The defense filings agree that the board voted again to close the main building, but they quote the timing differently. The statement of facts says it would close to patrons immediately; the supporting memorandum says closure would follow dissolution of the preliminary injunction.<sup class="src-ref">
   519	<a href="#src-28" data-record-href="/records/defendants-statement-facts-89-2-2026-09-18/" data-passage="shall be closed to patrons forthwith" aria-label="Source 28: read the evidence">28</a>
   520	</sup>

