 succeeded in 0ms:
   521	<sup class="src-ref">
   522	<a href="#src-27" data-record-href="/records/defendants-consolidated-memorandum-88-1-2026-09-18/" data-passage="forthwith upon the dissolution of the preliminary injunction" aria-label="Source 27: read the evidence">27</a>
   523	</sup>
   524	</p>
   525	<p data-layer="narrative">The defendants argued that phased closure would create a $300 million funding shortfall, compared with less than $30 million for full closure. These were the defendants' assertions. Floca's declaration identifies an earlier JLL plan and Delta presentation as filed under seal. It says the finalized Delta report and certain appendices were attached as Exhibit A, while appendices with sensitive architectural drawings were excluded.<sup class="src-ref">
   526	<a href="#src-27" data-record-href="/records/defendants-consolidated-memorandum-88-1-2026-09-18/" data-passage="a $300 million funding shortfall" aria-label="Source 27: read the evidence">27</a>
   527	</sup>
   528	<sup class="src-ref">
   529	<a href="#src-29" data-record-href="/records/floca-declaration-89-3-2026-09-18/" data-passage="appears under seal on the docket" aria-label="Source 29: read the evidence" data-passages="correct copy of that report and certain of its appendices is attached to this declaration as&#10;appendices that contain sensitive architectural drawings">29</a>
   530	</sup>
   531	</p>
   532	<p data-layer="narrative">Later on September 18, thousands joined the Hands Around the Kennedy Center protest, and some formed a human chain around the building. The organizer invited artists, patrons, staff members, union members and volunteers.<sup class="src-ref">
   533	<a href="#src-33" data-record-href="/records/ap-kennedy-center-protest-2026-09-18/" data-passage="Thousands of people joined outside" aria-label="Source 33: read the evidence" data-passages="formed a human chain around the center">33</a>
   534	</sup>
   535	<sup class="src-ref">
   536	<a href="#src-34" data-record-href="/records/action-network-hands-around-kennedy-center-2026-09-18/" data-passage="Worked at the Center as a staff member, union member, or volunteer" aria-label="Source 34: read the evidence">34</a>
   537	</sup>
   538	</p>
   539	</section>
   540	<section id="unknowns">
   541	<p class="sec-kicker" data-layer="narrative">Open questions</p>
   542	<h2 data-layer="fact">What we do not know yet</h2>
   543	<ul data-layer="fact">
   544	<li data-absence>Whether the September 23 status report was filed, and whether the initial safety closure was extended. Searched: the admitted docket material and coverage through September 19; the report was not yet due.</li>
   545	<li data-absence>Whether the defendants have developed a project-scope change that would trigger the notice order. The accessible public filings through September 19 do not identify an approved demolition plan. Floca's declaration identifies an earlier JLL report and Delta presentation filed under seal. It says the finalized Delta report and certain appendices were filed as Exhibit A, but that exhibit did not answer through the public docket route.</li>
   546	<li data-absence>Which closure condition appears in the September 15 preliminary minutes. The two defense filings quote the resolution differently, and the preliminary minutes were not available through the public docket route.</li>
   547	<li>Trump's intent remained unresolved on September 18. The Associated Press reported that he did not directly respond when asked whether he planned to demolish the theater.<sup class="src-ref">
   548	<a href="#src-35" data-record-href="/records/ap-trump-kennedy-center-2026-09-18/" data-passage="did not directly respond when a reporter asked whether he planned to demolish the theater" aria-label="Source 35: read the evidence">35</a>
   549	</sup>
   550	</li>
   551	<li data-absence>The court's minute order as a standalone, court-hosted document. Searched: the District Court docket, CourtListener and Justia; the docket routes were unavailable to the capture registry and the Justia mirror stopped before September 17. The page therefore labels the carriers of the quoted sentence.</li>
   552	</ul>
   553	</section>
