data/sources/coverage/kennedy-center/article_0881.txt:3:Trump was seen with a placard that appeared to say, "Kennedy Center DEMOLISHED."
data/sources/coverage/kennedy-center/article_0881.txt:5:U.S. District Judge Christopher Cooper made his ruling the afternoon after President Donald Trump was photographed looking over a placard that appeared to include the words "Kennedy Center DEMOLISHED" over what appeared to be an image of a demolition.
data/sources/coverage/kennedy-center/article_0881.txt:9:The photos of Trump examining the placard were taken Wednesday night through a cabin window on Air Force One by Agence France-Presse photojournalist Brendan Smialowski, who was acting as the pool photographer for White House coverage, as Trump landed at Joint Base Andrews.
data/sources/coverage/kennedy-center/article_0881.txt:10:It was not immediately clear what the full contents of the placard were or how they were generated. The published images don't show the entire placard and the word that appears to be "DEMOLISHED" was not entirely visible, cut off as "DEMOLIS."
data/sources/kennedy-center/beatty-reply-87-2026-09-17.txt:354:ripped down.4 Separately, images on social media depict him reading a placard on Air Force One
