WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
The safety is of
the utmost concern

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.320
of our chairman, the president.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.440
And we will make sure that
there is a path forward

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.660
for this institution.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.940
It will move forward.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.340
Nothing is being demolished.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.600
Ignore the media
that is saying that,

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.040
because no one has
ever said that coming

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.220
from the institution.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.840
I can promise you that.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.400
We are building more.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.660
We are adding, not subtracting.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.320
And that's the goal
of this president.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.790
"Nothing is being demolished."

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.040
That's the message from a
spokesperson for the Kennedy

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:30.540
Center.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.480
But that comes after President
Trump said it would end up

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.480
being, quote, "ripped down."

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:38.640
And these are photos appearing
to show the president looking

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.780
at a document that says
"Kennedy Center demolished."

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.120
Lawmakers are weighing
in on the possibility.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.060
I'm confident that,
one way or the other,

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.440
whether it's legislatively
or whether it's legally

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.400
in the courts, we're going
to stop the president

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:59.800
from another vanity project
and waste of taxpayer resources

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.080
in the context of
the Kennedy Center.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.200
Let's bring in politics
reporter for CBS News

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.540
Digital, Kathryn Watson.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.100
Kathryn, always
great to be with you.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.310
What else is the
president saying here?

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:11.690
Well, the Kennedy
Center board,

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.130
to back up a little bit,
which is run by Trump allies,

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.230
says the venue is
facing financial ruin

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.310
and that the center has
to have President Trump's

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.750
name on the building to
raise the money it needs.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.170
That is their argument.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.590
Yesterday, the president
said his administration

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.470
should be recognized for
the building with his name.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.210
And if that doesn't
happen, he said

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:32.110
the building may be forced to
shut down because, he says,

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.470
it's in disrepair.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.310
Let's hear what he said about
that yesterday on the campaign

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.790
trail in North Carolina.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.430
So for the Trump
administration, for me,

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:46.350
to get involved and to take that
on long term, and to carry it,

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.990
or to raise money
to carry it, I think

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.550
that the Trump administration
should certainly

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:52.750
have recognition.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.475
Because, frankly, if we don't
do that, it's going to close.

00:01:56.475 --> 00:01:57.850
It will end up
being ripped down.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.330
It's in very, very bad
shape, very dangerous shape.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.850
You see steel falling down.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:04.330
You see plaster
falling off ceilings.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:05.870
You see a lot of dangerous--

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:10.862
it's been very badly
maintained for 25 years.

00:02:10.862 --> 00:02:13.070
But there are legal battles
over the Kennedy Center

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.470
that the Trump
administration has

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:16.990
had to grapple with in court.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:18.910
And, Kathryn, new
details are coming out

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.510
of court documents
about what a witness saw

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.850
outside that building.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.170
What are we learning there?

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:25.670
Yeah.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.890
So there is an ongoing lawsuit
from Congresswoman Joyce Beatty,

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.030
who is an ex-officio
Kennedy Center board

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.990
member, because she's
a member of Congress.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.590
And that lawsuit is trying
to stop the president's name

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.850
from going on the building.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.790
Now, as a part of
that, new documents

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.070
were filed in that
lawsuit yesterday.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.150

